      },
      "text": "Egyptian religion is one of the world's longest-lived: 3,000+ years from c. 3000 BCE to 392 CE (Theodosius closes pagan temples). It produced the **oldest religious texts in the world** (Pyramid Texts, 2400 BCE), an extraordinarily complex theology, and the most elaborate system of afterlife preparation in any ancient culture."
    },
    {
      "id": "05-EGYPTIAN.md#003",
      "path": [
        "05-EGYPTIAN.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:mythology:05-egyptian, git-history:mythology:05-egyptian]",
        "canonical_path": "mythology/05-EGYPTIAN.md",
        "concepts": "[egyptian]",
        "current_path": "mythology/05-EGYPTIAN.md",
        "id": "maxim:mythology:egyptian",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "mythology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[egyptian]",
        "section": "mythology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Egyptian Mythology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│              EGYPTIAN COSMOLOGICAL SCHOOLS                       │\n│                                                                  │\n│  HELIOPOLIS (On):                                                │\n│  The Ennead — \"Nine\" — the primary creation theology             │\n│  Atum → Shu+Tefnut → Geb+Nut → Osiris+Isis+Set+Nephthys          │\n│  Ra/Atum as sun-creator; solar theology dominant                 │\n│                                                                  │\n│  MEMPHIS:                                                        │\n│  Ptah creates through thought (heart) and word (tongue)          │\n│  = intellectual/ideational creation; proto-Logos theology        │\n│  \"Memphite Theology\" (Shabaka Stone, ~700 BCE, claims older)     │\n│                                                                  │\n│  HERMOPOLIS:                                                     │\n│  The Ogdoad — \"Eight\" primordial pairs (chaos before creation)   │\n│  Nun+Naunet (water), Amun+Amaunet (hidden), Huh+Hauhet (infinity)│\n│  Kuk+Kauket (darkness) — the eight chaos forces                  │\n│  Creation: primordial mound rises from chaos waters; first light │\n│                                                                  │\n│  THEBES (New Kingdom dominance):                                 │\n│  Amun becomes \"king of gods\"; syncretized as Amun-Ra             │\n│  Eventually: \"the hidden one\" whose name cannot be spoken        │\n│  → proto-monotheistic trend                                      │\n│                                                                  │\n│  AMARNA HERESY (Akhenaten, 1353–1336 BCE):                       │\n│  Akhenaten (Amenhotep IV) suppresses all gods → worship Aten only│\n│  (solar disk, not anthropomorphized)                             │\n│  Only documented attempt at royal-imposed monotheism             │\n│  Reversed immediately after Akhenaten's death                    │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```"
    },
